                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "@bdillahu, I believe this is the answer here. There is a call to [`MiniMisc.setup_auto_root()`](https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/blob/f76d787a7be141b311d7afd2cfd14b94133bcdf8/configs/nvim-0.12/plugin/30_mini.lua#L249-L253), which automatically adjusts Neovim's working directory to be a project root. So in a sense, `:n <filename>` *does* search it in the current directory.\r\n\r\nCould you please check if removing `setup_auto_root()` makes it work as you expect?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAuto-root type functionality was one of the first things I added when started my Neovim journey and I can not imagine using Neovim without it. In particular, because it makes it very ergonomic working with files from different projects.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">@bdillahu, I believe this is the answer here. There is a call to <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/blob/f76d787a7be141b311d7afd2cfd14b94133bcdf8/configs/nvim-0.12/plugin/30_mini.lua#L249-L253\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniMisc.setup_auto_root()</code></a>, which automatically adjusts Neovim's working directory to be a project root. So in a sense, <code class=\"notranslate\">:n &lt;filename&gt;</code> <em>does</em> search it in the current directory.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Could you please check if removing <code class=\"notranslate\">setup_auto_root()</code> makes it work as you expect?</p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Auto-root type functionality was one of the first things I added when started my Neovim journey and I can not imagine using Neovim without it. In particular, because it makes it very ergonomic working with files from different projects.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "@bdillahu, I believe this is the answer here. There is a call to MiniMisc.setup_auto_root(), which automatically adjusts Neovim's working directory to be a project root. So in a sense, :n <filename> does search it in the current directory.\nCould you please check if removing setup_auto_root() makes it work as you expect?\n\nAuto-root type functionality was one of the first things I added when started my Neovim journey and I can not imagine using Neovim without it. In particular, because it makes it very ergonomic working with files from different projects.",
